   - Second term: $\mathbf{j} \times [(\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{k}) \times \mathbf{j}]$ simplifies to $(\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{k}) - (\mathbf{j} \cdot (\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{k}))\mathbf{j}$.  
   - Third term: $\mathbf{k} \times [(\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{i}) \times \mathbf{k}]$ simplifies to $(\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{i}) - (\mathbf{k} \cdot (\mathbf{v} - \mathbf{i}))\mathbf{k}$.  
